  "summary": "I’m a Software Engineer at PURVIS Systems with a Bachelor’s degree in Software Engineering from the New England Institute of Technology.\n\nMy professional experience includes software development, systems integration, troubleshooting, testing, and deployment of mission-critical technology within the public safety industry. I work with Fire Station Alerting Systems (FSAS), Computer-Aided Dispatch (CAD) integration, networking, and server-based environments supporting emergency response operations.\n\nMy technical background includes C#, .NET, C++, JavaScript, SQL, Git, Azure DevOps, and Windows Server. I also utilize AI-assisted development tools, including Claude Code, to support software development, debugging, and technical problem-solving.\n\nI enjoy tackling complex technical challenges, improving existing applications, identifying and resolving software issues, and developing practical solutions that improve functionality, reliability, and efficiency.\n\nOpen to Freelance, Part-Time & Contract Opportunities\n\nAlongside my full-time engineering career, I’m interested in collaborating with individuals, startups, and businesses on independent software development projects.\n\nMy areas of interest include:\n\n* Software debugging and troubleshooting\n* Application maintenance and enhancements\n* Website and web application development\n* Desktop application development\n* Custom scripting and workflow automation\n* Short-term software development contracts\n\nI value clear communication, attention to detail, and delivering reliable solutions that meet project requirements.\n\nWhether you need help resolving an existing software issue, improving an application, or developing something new, I’m open to discussing opportunities where my technical experience can provide value.\n\nFeel free to connect or message me to discuss a potential project.",
