    "description": "Software Engineer specializing in the development, maintenance, integration, and support of mission-critical public safety technology, including Fire Station Alerting Systems (FSAS) used by emergency response organizations. \n\nMy responsibilities span software development, troubleshooting, system testing, deployment, and technical support across interconnected software, hardware, and server environments.\n\nKey Responsibilities & Contributions: \nDevelop, enhance, and maintain software applications using C#, C++, and .NET technologies.\nDesign and implement new application features, resolve software defects, and improve existing functionality and system reliability.\nSupport Fire Station Alerting Systems (FSAS) and their integration with Computer-Aided Dispatch (CAD) platforms.\nInvestigate and manage technical support tickets, diagnose complex issues, identify root causes, and implement effective solutions.\nPerform software deployments, application updates, and patches across customer server environments.\nTroubleshoot software, networking, and server-related issues to maintain dependable system operations.\nParticipate in system integration, testing, configuration, installation, and field deployment activities.\nCollaborate with engineering teams using Agile/Scrum methodologies and Git-based version control workflows.\nUtilize modern development tools, including Azure DevOps, SourceTree, and Claude Code, to support software engineering and technical problem-solving.\n\nTechnologies & Tools: \nC#, C++, .NET, JavaScript, SQL, Git, Azure DevOps, SourceTree, Windows Server, Claude Code, FSAS, CAD Integration, Agile/Scrum.",
